# Pre-v1 hard cuts

Ze has never been deployed. Until a versioned v1 is declared, breaking changes
are the default.

- Do not add compatibility shims, deprecated aliases, dual-write, or dual-read
  so that old callers keep working. Update in-tree callers in the same change.
- Do not keep a second vocabulary for the same concept to avoid a migration.
- "Don't break existing data" is not a valid objection. Local and seed
  databases may be wiped and remigrated.
- Wrap-then-replace is forbidden as a multi-phase strategy.

This does not skip spec-first development, and it does not license inventing
contribution arbitration or merging the loop and goal stores.

Authoritative text: `.specify/memory/constitution.md` Principle VIII and
`specs/arch/pre-v1-hard-cuts.md`.
